Cutfile is a simple utility that restricts the size of a file to a given
number of lines.  This is useful for keeping your log files from getting
too large.  To run Cutfile:

Cutfile <pattern> <max. lines>

Where the pattern is a filename and can include AmigaDOS wildcards.  The
file(s) matching the pattern are scanned and cut if they are longer than
the maximum allowed number of lines.  It is a good idea to have this run
automatically once a day (or even more often, if you wish).
